# Cloudflare Pages — SPA routing for the two entries.
#
# /admin/* → serve the admin SPA's index.html (admin handles its own
#            hash routing internally for #pr / #vs / #shop / etc.)
# /*       → serve the public SPA's index.html (router in main.js
#            maps the path to a tab — /news, /pr, /vssound, /shop,
#            /tools, /about, /news/{id} for individual articles)
#
# Order matters: Cloudflare evaluates top→bottom and stops at the
# first match. /admin must be listed before /* so admin URLs don't
# fall through to the public SPA.
#
# /passport/* needs NO rule, and that is the point of the repo merge.
#             Passport is built into dist/passport/ by `npm run build:passport`,
#             so real files exist at that path and Cloudflare serves a real file
#             ahead of the SPA catch-all below.
#
#             This used to point at a splash saying Passport was not in this
#             build — true then, because a preview built only this repo. The
#             premise is gone, and with it the second preview URL and the second
#             login it forced: /passport/ is now the SAME ORIGIN as the site
#             around it, so one sign-in covers both.
#
#             ⛔ Do not add a /passport rule back. A rule here would shadow the
#             real files, and the catch-all must never be allowed to answer
#             /passport/* — that is what made the Passport button silently open
#             the public app again (reported 2026-08-31).
#             ⚠️ Cloudflare only — nginx never reads this file and keeps serving
#             /passport/ from its own location block. Production is untouched.

/admin/*     /admin/index.html          200
/*           /index.html                200
